  ($$forearm_mappings_v1$$, $$cat-132:forearm.br$$, $$cat-132$$, $$forearm.br$$, $$elbow.flexion$$, $$direct$$, $$dynamic$$, $$inference$$, $$individual$$, false, $$Hammer-style curls keep the forearm in neutral, where the brachioradialis lies well placed to flex the elbow, and they are the usual choice to train it, so it is a direct target here. EMG studies disagree on how much its activity changes with forearm position (M1 found the change in pronation), so 'direct' is a judgement about the exercise's purpose, not a measured larger share.$$, $$reviewed$$),
