  ($$forearm_mappings_v1$$, $$cat-408:forearm.ecu$$, $$cat-408$$, $$forearm.ecu$$, $$wrist.ulnar_deviation$$, $$direct$$, $$dynamic$$, $$anatomy$$, $$shared$$, false, $$Tilting the hand toward the pinky side is done by the flexor and extensor on that side together, so each is direct and the work is shared; how the split moves with a slightly flexed or extended wrist is not known, so no split is given.$$, $$reviewed$$),
