  ($$forearm_mappings_v1$$, $$cat-78:forearm.fdp$$, $$cat-78$$, $$forearm.fdp$$, $$fingers.dip_flexion$$, $$contributing$$, $$isometric$$, $$inference$$, $$shared$$, true, $$Pulling on a towel or rope closes the fist around a thick, soft handle and the grip often limits the set, so the finger flexors are contributing rather than merely incidental; the work is still not the purpose of a timed hold, and it is shared between FDS and FDP. A strapped set earns no grip credit.$$, $$reviewed$$),
